{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch8BSeWgbS7sVScBJNCyz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Approve.** The change adds no authority.\n\n**Capabilities.** Before and after, `load`, `apply` and `save` take only plain data (`&[u8]`, `&mut Inventory`, `&Inventory`). None of them holds a capability, and the trust diff is empty, which agrees.\n\n**What the new code does.** It adds two `ApplyError` variants (lines 35–38) and two new match arms in `apply`:\n\n- Lines 65–67 return `ZeroQuantity(sku)` for a `Restock` or `Sell` of 0.\n- Lines 80–82 return `AlreadyDiscontinued(sku)` when the item's `discontinued == Some(true)`.\n\nBoth arms work only on in-memory data. Neither prints anything, so no data goes to the output sinks.\n\n**Inventory left unchanged on failure.** `apply` works on a clone (`next`, line 52) and writes it back to `*inv` only on success (line 86). An early `return Err(...)` therefore leaves the inventory unchanged, as the description says.\n\n**New error data.** The new errors carry only the SKU, the same data that `UnknownSku`, `Insufficient` and `Overflow` already return to the caller. Nothing is exposed that wasn't before.\n\n```json\n{\"verdict\": \"approve\", \"findings\": []}\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4188,"cache_read_input_tokens":1630,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4188},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7742e5be-f05f-4a31-a7f3-bfa9b2abecbe","uuid":"f63e7faf-05a3-47de-8d9f-bdeb7a7c658e","timestamp":"2026-11-17T08:25:32.041Z","request_id":"req_011Ch8BSePk5n6adzoK9BHdP"}
